<title>FRANCE: Cold snap hits rail services in southern France.</title>
<headline>Cold snap hits rail services in southern France.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>French rail services were badly disrupted in the south of the country on Thursday as snow and ice stuck to overhead lines, the SNCF rail board said.</p>
<p>Passenger and freight services were suspended between Valance and Avignon and north-south traffic to the south of France's second city, Lyon, was delayed for up to three hours.</p>
<p>The problems were caused by ice on the overhead electric cables used to power the trains, the SNCF said.</p>
<p>The nine-day-old cold snap, which has sent temperatures plunging across Europe, is expected to last into the weekend.</p>
</text>
